From: George Whewell <georgerw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: sophgo: size VPSS queue data for V4L2 type indices

The driver indexes queue state using V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE (1)
and V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT (2). A two-element array puts every OUTPUT
access beyond the array and on top of the capture crop. Reserve all three
indices so source geometry and crop cannot overwrite each other.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c
index c4fa6bf..99f0a7c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/sophgo/sg2002-vpss.c
@@ -176,7 +176,8 @@ struct vpss_dev {
 struct vpss_ctx {
 	struct v4l2_fh		fh;
 	struct vpss_dev		*dev;
-	struct vpss_q_data	q_data[2];	/* [OUTPUT]=src, [CAPTURE]=dst */
+	/* Indexed by enum v4l2_buf_type: CAPTURE is 1, OUTPUT is 2. */
+	struct vpss_q_data	q_data[V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_OUTPUT + 1];
 	/* CAPTURE-side crop: the visible image inside the (possibly
 	 * macroblock-padded) CAPTURE surface.  The scaler produces the
 	 * crop geometry; the format geometry only sets the plane layout
